Python example: a simple offline binary mutation lab.

```python
import random

original = bytearray(b"\x45\x00\x00\x28")

def mutate(data):
    result = bytearray(data)

    position = random.randrange(len(result))
    result[position] ^= 1 << random.randrange(8)

    return result

for i in range(10):
    print(mutate(original).hex())
```

This modifies sample bytes in memory. It does not send traffic or attack a remote system.

